1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,070
- So there's a few
things going on here.

2
00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:06,940
The cold water rapidly cools the
exterior surface of the glass,

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,142
hardening it almost immediately.

4
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:12,613
The interior, still
molten, cools more slowly.

5
00:00:12,613 --> 00:00:15,782
As it cools, it contracts and
attempts to pull the surface

6
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:17,718
in with it, but it can't--

7
00:00:17,718 --> 00:00:19,219
well, not very much.

8
00:00:19,219 --> 00:00:20,888
The surface has
already hardened,

9
00:00:20,888 --> 00:00:23,891
so it gets pulled in only
a little, compressing it,

10
00:00:23,891 --> 00:00:27,427
while also creating an internal
layer that remains forever

11
00:00:27,427 --> 00:00:29,496
under tension.

12
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:31,198
It is this action
that gives the glass

13
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:33,166
its uncharacteristic strength.

14
00:00:33,166 --> 00:00:36,603
We call it compressive strength.

15
00:00:36,603 --> 00:00:38,071
- It sounds like
the same principle

16
00:00:38,071 --> 00:00:41,241
as how an arch provides strength
in structural engineering.

17
00:00:41,241 --> 00:00:42,309
- Yes, kind of.

18
00:00:42,309 --> 00:00:44,111
Now, Jamie, I'm going
to ask for your help.

19
00:00:44,111 --> 00:00:46,546
We're going to attempt to
destroy this Prince Rupert

20
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:47,247
drop.

21
00:00:47,247 --> 00:00:50,350
I just want you to tip that
hammer past its center point.

22
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:50,884
Go ahead.

23
00:00:54,488 --> 00:00:55,989
That's what Peter
was talking about.

24
00:00:55,989 --> 00:00:57,591
So you can hit it really hard.

25
00:00:57,591 --> 00:00:59,593
- Now I feel like
we've been swindled.

26
00:00:59,593 --> 00:01:00,727
- Swindled not.

27
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:01,795
We have just experienced--

28
00:01:01,795 --> 00:01:02,896
That's good writing.

29
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:03,730
That's good writing.

30
00:01:03,730 --> 00:01:05,299
- --the power of
compressive strength.

31
00:01:05,299 --> 00:01:07,100
It does, however,
have an Achilles heel.

32
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:12,072
Take those nippers right
there and nip the backside

33
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:14,074
of the tail of this
Prince Rupert drop

34
00:01:14,074 --> 00:01:15,042
and watch what happens.

35
00:01:15,042 --> 00:01:16,743
Wait, wait, wait, cue
the high-speed camera.

36
00:01:16,743 --> 00:01:17,444
OK, here we go.

37
00:01:21,848 --> 00:01:22,349
- Oh!

38
00:01:25,485 --> 00:01:26,053
Here it comes.

39
00:01:31,291 --> 00:01:33,827
- That was even cooler
than I thought it would be.

40
00:01:33,827 --> 00:01:34,795
[END PLAYBACK]

41
00:01:34,795 --> 00:01:37,064
So that's what
you just saw live.

42
00:01:37,064 --> 00:01:40,467
And what that is is
it's a relief of--

43
00:01:40,467 --> 00:01:41,768
thank you, or not.

44
00:01:41,768 --> 00:01:42,736
[APPLAUSE]

45
00:01:42,736 --> 00:01:43,337
Yeah, sure.
